- Import slugify from 'slugify'
- Add MAX_SLUG_LENGTH = 50 constant
- Add --title argument parsing (required for slug generation)
- Generate slug using slugify(title, { lower: true, strict: true })
- Truncate slug to MAX_SLUG_LENGTH characters
- Return nextId in format "{paddedNumber}-{slug}"
- Add slug field to output JSON
- Handle missing --title: return error JSON with usage message

Current code (lines 81-92):
```typescript
// Find highest ID (folder names are "001", "002", etc.)
let highest = 0;
for (const folderName of folders) {
  const id = parseInt(folderName, 10);
